ept.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":1174,"Y":744},"LeftTop":{"X":1174,"Y":711},"RightBottom":{"X":1668,"Y":744},"RightTop":{"X":1668,"Y":711}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":27,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Metropolitan University","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":1273,"Y":782},"LeftTop":{"X":1273,"Y":749},"RightBottom":{"X":1570,"Y":782},"RightTop":{"X":1570,"Y":749}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":28,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Sylhet, Bangladesh","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":1302,"Y":820},"LeftTop":{"X":1302,"Y":785},"RightBottom":{"X":1541,"Y":820},"RightTop":{"X":1541,"Y":785}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":29,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"rakibulislamrafi36@gmail.com","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":1238,"Y":858},"LeftTop":{"X":1238,"Y":823},"RightBottom":{"X":1616,"Y":858},"RightTop":{"X":1616,"Y":823}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":30,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Abstract—Accurate leaf disease detection in indoor ornamental plants remains a critical challenge due to reliance on subjective visual inspection and the high cost of molecular diagnostics. This work addresses the need for an efficient and lightweight system to monitor plant health and prevent disease spread in controlled environments. The main objective is to develop and evaluate a comprehensive end-to-end detection model, based on modern YOLO architectures, to identify and localize nine disease and healthy classes across three species: Money Plant, Snake Plant, and Spider Plant. A custom dataset of 787 high-resolution images was collected under variable lighting and backgrounds, annotated and expanded to 3,935 images via systematic augmentation. Three variants-YOLOv8s, YOLOv9s, and the YOLOv11s were trained on 640×640 inputs with AdamW optimization and evaluated using Precision, Recall, mAP ![](842,1394,865,1425)50, and mAP ![](264,1425,286,1452)50-95. YOLOv11s achieved superior performance, recording 97.4% mAP ![](401,1456,428,1482)50, 89.3% mAP@50-95, 93.7% Precision, and 96.7% Recall on the held-out test set. Class-wise analysis revealed consistently high recall, with minor confusions among visually similar disease symptoms. To enhance interpretability, occlusion sensitivity and RISE (Randomized Input Sampling for Explanation) analyses were employed, confirming that the model focuses on disease-relevant leaf regions while suppressing background features. The YOLOv11s framework delivers an accurate and interpretable solution for indoor plant disease monitoring, enabling early diagnosis and timely intervention in ornamental plant care.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":144,"Y":1785},"LeftTop":{"X":144,"Y":979},"RightBottom":{"X":906,"Y":1785},"RightTop":{"X":906,"Y":979}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"images/c2eaf940a23966f305ef95bc1cbdb9d0-image.png","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":31,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Index Terms—indoor plant disease detection, object detection, yolov11, deep learning, machine learning, leaf disease","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":144,"Y":1847},"LeftTop":{"X":144,"Y":1787},"RightBottom":{"X":904,"Y":1847},"RightTop":{"X":904,"Y":1787}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":32,"Type":"title","Text":"##  I. INTRODUCTION","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":403,"Y":1920},"LeftTop":{"X":403,"Y":1892},"RightBottom":{"X":647,"Y":1920},"RightTop":{"X":647,"Y":1892}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":33,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Plant diseases cause substantial losses in agricultural productivity, directly affecting food security and farmer livelihoods [1]. Traditional detection methods, which rely on human expertise, are often subjective, error-prone, and inefficient when scaled to large farming systems. Advances in computer vision and deep learning (DL) have made automated plant dis-","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":144,"Y":2158},"LeftTop":{"X":144,"Y":1944},"RightBottom":{"X":902,"Y":2158},"RightTop":{"X":902,"Y":1944}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":34,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"ease detection a promising approach, offering rapid, accurate, and scalable solutions for practical applications. [2].","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":933,"Y":1046},"LeftTop":{"X":933,"Y":979},"RightBottom":{"X":1695,"Y":1046},"RightTop":{"X":1695,"Y":979}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":35,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Although several deep learning models have been applied in this domain, challenges persist due to limited datasets, lack of standardized annotations, and insufficient interpretability of model predictions. Many existing works focus on single architectures or small-scale datasets, limiting their generalizability to diverse environments. Furthermore, the \"black-box\" characteristics of deep neural networks remain a source of concern about trust and transparency in agricultural applications [3].","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":933,"Y":1331},"LeftTop":{"X":933,"Y":1048},"RightBottom":{"X":1695,"Y":1331},"RightTop":{"X":1695,"Y":1048}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":36,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Recent research has explored the use of advanced object detection architectures, such as the YOLO family, for multiclass leaf disease detection, demonstrating improved efficiency and accuracy in agricultural settings [4]. Building on this progress, the present study leverages YOLOv8s [5], YOLOv9s [6], and YOLOv11s [7] to address multi-class plant disease detection. A curated dataset of 787 images covering three plant species and nine distinct classes was carefully annotated and expanded through extensive preprocessing and augmentation techniques (resizing, flipping, rotation, zooming, and lighting variations), resulting in a final dataset of 3,935 images. Model training and evaluation were conducted using established metrics such as precision, recall, and mean average precision (mAP).","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":935,"Y":1794},"LeftTop":{"X":935,"Y":1333},"RightBottom":{"X":1695,"Y":1794},"RightTop":{"X":1695,"Y":1333}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":37,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"In addition, interpretability techniques such as occlusion [8] sensitivity and RISE [9] analysis were used to deliver deeper insights into model decision-making, ensuring reliability, practical applicability and Explainability [10]. Comparative analysis highlights the performance differences across YOLOv8s, YOLOv9s, and YOLOv11s, with particular emphasis on the improvements observed in YOLOv11s.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":933,"Y":2046},"LeftTop":{"X":933,"Y":1797},"RightBottom":{"X":1695,"Y":2046},"RightTop":{"X":1695,"Y":1797}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":38,"Type":"title","Text":"##  Objectives:","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":961,"Y":2079},"LeftTop":{"X":961,"Y":2046},"RightBottom":{"X":1113,"Y":2079},"RightTop":{"X":1113,"Y":2046}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":39,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"● Development of an augmented and annotated dataset for plant disease detection with improved diversity and","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":961,"Y":2158},"LeftTop":{"X":961,"Y":2084},"RightBottom":{"X":1695,"Y":2158},"RightTop":{"X":1695,"Y":2084}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":40,"Type":"footer","Text":"979-8-3315-7269-3/25/$31.00 ©2025 IEEE","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":146,"Y":2277},"LeftTop":{"X":146,"Y":2246},"RightBottom":{"X":680,"Y":2277},"RightTop":{"X":680,"Y":2246}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""}]}